# Supabase Data API grants

From 30 October 2026, Supabase does not grant Data API access to new tables in `public`. Existing tables keep their current grants.

When a migration creates a table in `public`, add the grant in that same migration, after the table exists:

```sql
grant select, insert, update, delete on table public.your_table to service_role;
```

Report-O-Matic reaches Postgres through the service role. Do not grant `anon` or `authenticated` unless the maintainer explicitly asks for that role to use the Data API on that table.

Row level security stays on. Grants decide whether the Data API can see the table. Policies decide which rows a role can touch.

The same rule applies to every Supabase project: a new `public` table is unreachable from `supabase-js`, PostgREST, and GraphQL until its migration grants the roles that should reach it.
